WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
 What's up, Marvel fans.

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.060
We're here with Chris
McKenna and Eric Sommers,

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.260
the writers of the film.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.270
You all have so much
to juggle in this.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.690
There are so many characters.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:08.490
Where do you even begin?

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.920
 We didn't know where to begin.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.060
We honestly, we--
after the last movie,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.030
there were a lot of different
things that we couldn't do,

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.620
and a lot of--

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:23.520
in a good way.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.280
I think those kind of
limitations are good,

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:31.080
but once the idea of the
multiverse opened up to us,

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.570
obviously there was an
infinite number of ways to go,

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:39.510
and almost an embarrassment of
riches in terms of what we had

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.420
to choose from, but
also restrain ourselves,

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.757
because we knew we
had to tell one story.

00:00:45.757 --> 00:00:46.890
 Yeah, I would
just say that with

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:51.060
the preceding two
spider-man movies, we always

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.530
had to-- and with this one--

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:57.090
we had some housekeeping to do,
dealing with the larger MCU,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.650
and other things
that had happened.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.130
And we had limitations
always, a lot

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.820
of which were fun to deal with.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.319
But in this one, in
addition to that,

00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:08.250
we then just had this door
open to the multiverse,

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.900
and just truly an infinite
number of possibilities.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:12.030
And it was almost overwhelming.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.000
And it took us a long time to
just talk and talk about it,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.210
and realize, like, what is the
most fun we could have with it?

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.740
And hopefully we did.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.030
 And with the
multiverse, we have

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.910
super villains from previous
spider-man films in this.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.730
What was it like to write
for those characters?

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.350
 Daunting.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.270
It was really daunting.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:33.870
You know, we had already watched
those movies so many times,

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.810
but now we had to
really watch them again,

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.870
and really try to live up to--

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.340
make sure we're living
up to the characters.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.710
But you know, I mean, Sam
Raimi is a hero of us,

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:47.290
and Marc Webb is an
incredible filmmaker.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:52.500
We wanted to do justice to the
worlds that they had created,

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.420
but also make sure that they fit
into the world that, you know,

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.480
that we've been so
honored to be a part of.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.380
So it was a juggling
act, you know.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.310
It really was.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:04.110
 It's funny.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:07.080
You know, the previous
spider-man movies

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.930
are movies that I would find
myself quoting with friends,

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:12.390
or just in a room with
writers discussing

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:13.620
something for reference.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.750
And this is the first time
where suddenly in my career

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.510
I was writing for
those characters

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.030
that I just thought were, like,
some kind of amazing reference,

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.500
or something I was a fan of.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.580
And yeah, it was daunting.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:24.420
It was daunting.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.040
But it was also
really, really fun.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.390
[MUSIC PLAYING]

